why does console.log show the old value right after i call setName?

const handleSubmit = () => {
  setName(input);
  console.log(name); // old value
};

Because `setName` doesn't change the `name` variable you're holding: it asks React to re-render, and only in that next render does `useState` return the new value. Inside the current call, `name` is still the value from the render that created `handleSubmit`.

If you need the new value in the same handler, use the value you already have:

```jsx
const handleSubmit = () => {
  setName(input);
  console.log(input); // the value you just set
  saveName(input);    // same here, don't read `name`
};
```

To see `name` after the update, log it in the component body, which runs on every render. Don't add a `useEffect` just to watch the change unless you need to sync with something outside React.

