Practical notes:

- `connect-src` must list every origin your `fetch`/XHR/WebSocket talks to, or API calls get blocked.
- Inline styles: some libraries inject them. Prefer moving to CSS files; if you can't, you'll need a nonce/hash or, as a last resort, `'unsafe-inline'` in `style-src` only (never in `script-src`).
- Avoid `'unsafe-inline'`/`'unsafe-eval'` in `script-src`. If a dependency needs `eval`, that's worth reconsidering.
- Set it as a real response header from your server/CDN, not just a `<meta>` tag (a meta CSP can't set `frame-ancestors`).

